y  starts telling Cassian everything he  knows about the prison this Sudden  Change proves Lutheran rail's theory he  tells more mothma in an earlier episode  that oppression breeds Rebellion show  people a clear way out without having to  fight and many will take it he argues  but but if you show people that there's  no way out they'll have no choice but to  take up arms that's exactly what Kino  seems primed to do  most of Andor episode 10 is spent on the  Kina 5 but there is a brief scene at the  ISB where major partagas gets briefed on  the agency's plan to trap a rebel cell  led by the enigmatic Anto Krieger the  ISB had captured a rebel pilot from  Krieger cell but released him back into  space dead in a malfunctioning ship to  assuage any concerns from the rebel  leader that the Empire might be onto his  plans patergas is informed that the ship  has been located as planned by caffeine  rescue Salvage a mining Outpost and  commerce Hub Catherine is where Cassian  first appears in Rogue one he follows up  a lead with a rebel contact there but  ends up killing the contact to secure  his Escape that escape is crucial as the  information he gets on Catherine  concerns the Death Star itself it  doesn't seem like the inclusion of  Catherine and Andor is of too much  specific importance but it is a nice bit  of connective tissue  and or episode 10 ends with a powerful  exchange between Luther and Rael and  Lani young his mole in the ISB we  learned that Lani has been periodically  given Lutheran information about  Imperial operations and that Lutheran  has shared some secrets about the rebels  to avoid suspicion when Lonnie says he  wants out Lutheran was spawned for the  powerful monologue listing all the  things he's given up to fight the Empire  I burned my decency for someone else's  future I burned my life to make a  sunrise that I know I'll Never See  it's a deeply affecting speech and this  magnified all the more by Lutheran's  Outfit Black robes beneath a flo