st designs for iconic  ships including the X-Wing and Tie  Fighter he also provided concepts for  the Imperial Star Destroyer which  initially bore the look of what's now  become the cantwell-class cruiser an  artist writer and engineer among other  things Cantwell worked with NASA and on  other major genre films like Stanley  Kubrick's 2001 A Space Odyssey its  initial design for the Stardust Joya was  meant to appear in Solo a Star Wars  story but the scene featuring it  prominently was curse you given how much  kanswell contributes it to the Star Wars  Universe it's nice to see his original  designer appear with such a Grandeur in  Andor  in the season finale the night before  Marva andor's funeral on ferricks  Deirdre Miro arrives via Lambda class  Imperial shuttle the stark white design  of the ship has been iconic since its  debut in the original trilogy and it  looks just as austere as ever here  standing out against the planet's night  sky like a stormtrooper against a brick  wall daedra's shuttle isn't the only  familiar Imperial ship in the scene  however NASA transport touches down we  can see another shuttle parked on an  adjacent landing pad with four thin  Wings pointing up to the sky this second  shuttle a Zeta class is the same model  as the one used by Cassian and Jin urso  in Rogue one stolen from the Empire the  zeta-class shuttle becomes a flagship of  the Rogue one Squad since the vessel is  a pretty standard cargo ship used for  transporting troops in cargo his  presence on ferex shouldn't raise any  eyebrows but his inclusion also feels  like an intentional nod toward cassian's  future marva's funeral ends up being a  pivotal moment in both ferric's  resistance against the empire and  cassian's own internal Arc by the end of  the season finale he has fully given  himself to the rebel course and the ship  glimpsed in his early shot to Marx  apathy's now headed down  in The Season's third episode Marva  gives a warning to some of the corporate  